  "version": "1.0.0",
  "verification": "draft",
  "notes": [
    "Every identifier scheme is free text: no source the pack cites publishes a format for the Ghana Card number, the birth certificate number, the TIN or the SSNIT number.",
    "The 16 regions and their ISO 3166-2 codes are read from a secondary copy of the ISO table and are unconfirmed; no official Ghanaian region code list was fetched. The district (metropolitan, municipal or district assembly) is free text and no list is bundled.",
    "No statute was fetched for the public holidays. The seven days listed are the ones a secondary list shows as fixed or Easter-dated; the Public Holidays and Commemorative Days Act's text and its amendments were not read, so every holiday is a draft.",
    "Not modelled, because their dates and statuses changed between acts and no statute was read: Constitution Day, Republic Day, Founders' Day and Kwame Nkrumah Memorial Day, Farmers' Day (first Friday of December), Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha (declared each year).",
    "A holiday on a weekend is kept on that day here; the secondary list says the following Monday is usually declared, and the pack does not model those notices.",
    "Only the PAYE due day is modelled, from the Ghana Revenue Authority. The SSNIT and tier-two pension remittance days were not found in a fetched source."
  ],
  "sources": [
